<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Al Wajbah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Al Wajbah was fought in March 1893 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doha">Doha</a> between Qatari forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jassim-bin-muhammad-al-thani">Jassim bin Muhammad Al Thani</a> and an Ottoman expedition led by the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a>. Jassim's men defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and forced them to release the hostages they held. The victory is celebrated in Qatar as a founding moment of the state's independence.</p></div>
